From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haze <patches@haze.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:38:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Give Haze its own install identity on Windows

Why: The install mode decides the user data dir (%LOCALAPPDATA%\Haze), the
policy registry key, the AppUserModelID that groups taskbar windows, the
ProgIDs and URL scheme, and the CLSIDs of the COM servers Haze registers.
The registry key third-party tools use to trigger a profile reset moves to
Software\Haze as well.
Sharing any of them with Chromium makes the two overwrite each other's
registration. The class CLSIDs, Active Setup GUID and AppContainer SID prefix
are new random values; the interface IIDs stay, because they name interfaces
defined in the IDL files, not the product.
Security-relevant: yes
Security: The sandbox SID prefix names the AppContainers Haze's
sandboxed processes run in. A distinct prefix keeps them from sharing
containers with Chromium; the sandbox policy itself is unchanged.
Area: core
---
 .../profile_resetter/triggered_profile_resetter_win.cc |  2 +-
 chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h         | 56 +++++-----
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/profile_resetter/triggered_profile_resetter_win.cc b/chrome/browser/profile_resetter/triggered_profile_resetter_win.cc
index bcc99b6..9ce3ddf 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/profile_resetter/triggered_profile_resetter_win.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/profile_resetter/triggered_profile_resetter_win.cc
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 #if BUILDFLAG(GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING)
 #define PRODUCT_NAME L"Google\\Chrome"
 #elif BUILDFLAG(CHROMIUM_BRANDING)
-#define PRODUCT_NAME L"Chromium"
+#define PRODUCT_NAME L"Haze"
 #else
 #error Unknown branding
 #endif
